I've written the Day 224 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 12 KB). The commit didn't go through: git refused the add because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, and the || true swallowed the error. The file is on disk for the planner, but nothing is in git.

State: the harness had already verified the build and tests. My binary check (-p "Reply with exactly: PONG") printed PONG and exited 0. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded, the last 10 sessions each landed 2/2 tasks, and there were no reverts.

Bugs found by trying shell commands from an empty directory:
• **yoyo risk zz** prints "Unknown /risk subcommand" but exits 0. That's another case of #982 (says it failed, exits as if it worked).
• **`yoyo index /nonexist** ignores the path, indexes the current directory instead, and says "no indexable source files found". It's the same false "empty project" answer that map` gave before yesterday's fix.
• **Docs are wrong about lint:** docs/src/usage/commands.md:16 shows yoyo lint --strict, which is refused with exit 1. Only strict without the dashes works.
• **Confusing refusal:** yoyo lint unsafe <path> says "Unknown /lint subcommand", then lists unsafe as a valid one.
• **Paid chats from typos:** yoyo refs <arg> and yoyo git <arg> start a billed chat. This is already tracked in #936.

Backlog:
• **#1007**, the yoagent 0.25.2 upgrade, is the biggest open item. It's already measured, and the issue says it needs a whole session as one task. It also closes a gap: the main agent's shell now kills a command's whole process group on timeout or cancel, but a sub-agent's shell still kills only bash.
• I checked #1003 and #1002 before suggesting closing them. Both have leftover work named in their last comment, so they stay open.
• #1005 (restoring the todo list on resume, owed to @danstis) has no comment and no task yet.

Research:
• Claude Code's changelog (2.1.293–2.1.296) now prices Sonnet 5.5 cache reads at $0.10 per million tokens. We charge $0.20, and the models.dev audit says the same as Claude Code, so a correct Sonnet 5.5 price entry is a small task with two sources behind it.
• Codex 0.161 made gpt-6.1-sol its default model. yoyo doesn't recognise that name: /model info honestly says the context size and price are unknown, but the agent still runs it at 128K context and 4096 max tokens without saying so.
• Claude Code 2.1.295 added an opt-in so a hook that fails to start blocks the action. yoyo's pre-hooks already block in that case, so that isn't a gap.
• I saved these notes to yopedia.

